#
# Worked example: the LIVE EXECUTION of the memory MCP triad as Transaction-Logic transactions.
#
# Where examples/trajectory-audit.ttl shows the READ-ONLY audit of an already-recorded
# trajectory, this file shows the EXECUTE path: each memory WRITE tool (store_claim,
# revise_belief) runs THROUGH the Transaction-Logic engine, and the executional-entailment
# verdict gates the commit. This is a worked illustration of the shape the native server
# (crates/mcp/src/lib.rs) produces; the byte-exact engine goldens live in
# conformance/logic/cases/transaction/memory-triad-execute/.
#
# TWO LAYERS, kept distinct below:
#   * The REQUEST the server builds INTERNALLY to drive the engine — the governing contract, its
#     logic:executionMode, and the start-state preconditions. This is assembled into the
#     transaction world (mcp.rs::txn_world_nquads) and is NOT persisted to memory.gts.
#   * The PERSISTED AUDIT CONTEXT the server writes ONTO each committed gmeow:ToolCall
#     (mcp.rs::write_audit_segment), so the turn is afterwards verifiable by the read-only
#     trajectory audit. Each committed call gets its OWN per-call anchor — the server mints
#     <call>#turn and <call>#start from that call's id (one anchor per call, not a shared turn).
#
# THREE EXECUTION BEHAVIOURS (all backed by the one engine):
#   * COMMIT — a write whose precondition obtains runs under logic:CommittedExecution: the verdict
#     succeeds, the effect is materialized, the claim is written, and the audit context is
#     persisted onto the call. The committed gmeow:toolResult carries the transaction verdict
#     ({"committed": true, "succeeded": true, "path_len": N}). This is ex:callStore / ex:callRevise.
#   * ROLLBACK is COMPENSATION, not deletion — revise_belief IS store_claim's logic:compensation
#     (declared in mcp-action-policy.ttl). A committed revise SUPPRESSES the stored claim
#     (logic:del retires it via the supersession quartet); the bytes are never erased (Principle
#     10). Re-storing (store_claim, revise_belief's own compensation) re-asserts it.
#   * SANDBOX (dry run) — a write may be tested under logic:HypotheticalExecution: the same
#     verdict is computed, the effect substrate is DISCARDED, and the response carries a
#     content-addressed logic:executedHypotheticallyAs witness. NOTHING is persisted — the server
#     returns before recording, so a dry run leaves no gmeow:ToolCall and no audit segment.
#
# EPISTEMIC SHAPE (recording vs. supplied audit context), exactly as trajectory-audit.ttl:
#   * The RECORDING is what the harness captured per call: gmeow:usedTool, gmeow:toolArguments /
#     gmeow:toolResult, gmeow:atTime, gmeow:eventTemporalFrame.
#   * The AUDIT CONTEXT is layered on to make the turn checkable: logic:instantiatesSchema (a TRUE
#     tool-contract fact — calling store_claim instantiates the store_claim action schema in
#     mcp-action-policy.ttl), the per-call logic:properPartOf anchor, and the anchor's
#     logic:transitionFromState start state bearing the preconditions that obtained.
#
# This binds to the REAL mcp-action-policy.ttl schemas (mcp:storeClaim / mcp:reviseBelief) — no
# re-minted schema individuals; their logic:precondition / logic:effect / logic:compensation are
# the single authority. The slice does not reason its examples, so this file is a worked
# illustration only.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix mcp:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/mcp-policy/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# --- Agents: the model and the two tools the recording names. ---
ex:assistant a gmeow:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "assistant model agent"@x-gmeow-english .

ex:storeClaimTool a gmeow:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "memory store_claim tool"@x-gmeow-english .

ex:reviseBeliefTool a gmeow:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "memory revise_belief tool"@x-gmeow-english .

# ============================================================================================
# REQUEST LAYER (assembled into the transaction world, NOT persisted to memory.gts).
# The governing contract selects the execution mode the engine runs each write under.
# ============================================================================================

ex:committedContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    rdfs:label "commit the executed effects"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:executionMode logic:CommittedExecution .

ex:hypotheticalContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    rdfs:label "test without committing (sandbox)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:executionMode logic:HypotheticalExecution .

# ============================================================================================
# COMMITTED CALL 1 — store_claim under logic:CommittedExecution.
# RECORDING: usedTool + args + result (with the transaction verdict) + time + frame.
# AUDIT CONTEXT: instantiatesSchema (the true contract) + properPartOf this call's OWN anchor.
# ============================================================================================
ex:callStore a gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:label "store_claim (committed)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:usedTool ex:storeClaimTool ;
    gmeow:toolArguments "{\"text\": \"the GTS spec mandates RFC 8949 deterministic encoding\"}" ;
    gmeow:toolResult "{\"ok\": true, \"claim\": {\"id\": \"c-2300\"}, \"transaction\": {\"committed\": true, \"succeeded\": true, \"path_len\": 2}}" ;
    gmeow:atTime "2026-06-30T09:15:03Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    gmeow:eventTemporalFrame gmeow:temporalFrameUTCGregorian ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema mcp:storeClaim ;
    logic:properPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callStore#turn> .

# The per-call anchor the server mints (<call>#turn), bearing this call's start state (<call>#start).
# store_claim's precondition — a well-formed claim is presented — obtains at the start.
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callStore#turn>
    logic:transitionFromState <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callStore#start> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callStore#start>
    logic:situationObtains mcp:wellFormedClaim .

# The entity the store produced links BACK to its call (Principle 5: no forward output property).
ex:claim-c2300 a gmeow:Document ;
    rdfs:label "stored memory claim c-2300"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ex:callStore ;
    gmeow:wasAttributedTo ex:assistant .

# ============================================================================================
# COMMITTED CALL 2 — revise_belief, store_claim's compensation. A committed revise SUPPRESSES the
# just-stored claim (logic:del, the supersession quartet); it never deletes (Principle 10).
# Its preconditions (the target claim exists, and is in memory) obtained, so the run committed.
# ============================================================================================
ex:callRevise a gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:label "revise_belief (committed — the rollback/compensation)"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:usedTool ex:reviseBeliefTool ;
    gmeow:toolArguments "{\"claim_id\": \"c-2300\", \"reason\": \"superseded by a sharper source\"}" ;
    gmeow:toolResult "{\"ok\": true, \"suppressed\": \"c-2300\", \"superseded_by\": null, \"transaction\": {\"committed\": true, \"succeeded\": true, \"path_len\": 2}}" ;
    gmeow:atTime "2026-06-30T09:15:07Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    gmeow:eventTemporalFrame gmeow:temporalFrameUTCGregorian ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema mcp:reviseBelief ;
    logic:properPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callRevise#turn> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callRevise#turn>
    logic:transitionFromState <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callRevise#start> .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/agentic/memory-triad-execute/callRevise#start>
    logic:situationObtains mcp:targetClaimExists ,
                           mcp:claimInMemory .

# ============================================================================================
# SANDBOX (dry-run) — the SAME store_claim action tested under logic:HypotheticalExecution.
# The verdict is computed and the response carries a logic:executedHypotheticallyAs witness, but
# NOTHING is persisted: the server returns before recording, so there is no gmeow:ToolCall and no
# audit segment for a dry run. Only the REQUEST the engine evaluates is shown here.
#   server response (not persisted):
#     {"ok": true, "dry_run": true, "transaction": {"committed": false, "succeeded": true, "witness": "<n3-witness>"}}
# ============================================================================================
ex:dryRunStart a logic:Situation ;
    rdfs:label "start state of the dry-run request"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:situationObtains mcp:wellFormedClaim .
